<title>BELGIUM: BANK IPPA RAISES THREE-YEAR SAVINGS BOND RATE.</title>
<headline>BANK IPPA RAISES THREE-YEAR SAVINGS BOND RATE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Ippa bank, a unit of</p>
<p>insurer Royale Belge , said on Tuesday it would raise</p>
<p>interest rates on its three-year bank savings certificates to</p>
<p>4.00 percent from 3.75 percent.</p>
<p>The new rate would take effect on Wednesday, the bank said</p>
<p>in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
